\title{medrev: A Reproducible Toolkit for Biomedical Literature Reviews}
\description{
An end-to-end workflow for topic-driven biomedical literature reviews. From a research question or a set of identifiers it searches the literature through the Europe PubMed Central REST service \url{https://europepmc.org/RestfulWebService}, which indexes all of 'PubMed' and 'MEDLINE', into a tidy record table with a stable schema. Records are de-duplicated, screening decisions are tracked with reasons, and every stage is logged so a 'PRISMA'-style flow of counts can be derived. Included open-access articles are resolved to a full-text PDF (Europe PMC full text, with optional 'Unpaywall' \url{https://unpaywall.org/} and publisher citation-metadata fallbacks) and downloaded with polite rate limiting and retries. Only open-access content is fetched; closed-access hits are reported, never scraped.
}
